#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:3
msgid "HTTP Method Spoofing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:5
msgid ""
"When working with HTML forms you can only use GET or POST HTTP verbs. In "
"most cases, this is just fine. However, to support REST-ful routing you "
"need to support other, more correct, verbs, like DELETE or PUT. Since the"
" browsers don't support this, CodeIgniter provides you with a way to "
"spoof the method that is being used. This allows you to make a POST "
"request, but tell the application that it should be treated as a "
"different request type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:10
msgid ""
"To spoof the method, a hidden input is added to the form with the name of"
" ``_method``. It's value is the HTTP verb that you want the request to "
"be::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:17
msgid ""
"This form is converted into a PUT request and is a true PUT request as "
"far as the routing and the IncomingRequest class are concerned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:20
msgid ""
"The form that you are using must be a POST request. GET requests cannot "
"be spoofed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/methodspoofing.rst:22
msgid ""
"Be sure to check your web server's configuration as some servers do not "
"support all HTTP verbs with the default configuration, and must have "
"additional packages enabled to work."
msgstr ""

